    {
      "id": "gxd3nw54i",
      "node_id": "node-term-insurance-recommendation-b0ba433c",
      "version_tag": "v1",
      "title": "Term Insurance Recommendation",
      "description": {
        "text": {
          "text": {
            "text": {
              "text": {
                "text": "Retrieves full policy texts for the top 3 shortlisted plans and builds a detailed term insurance recommendation prompt.\n\nThis node prepares a comprehensive prompt for an LLM to produce the single best term life insurance recommendation from a shortlist. It first parses the shortlisted policies (from the previous LLM output) to extract the names of the top three plans. For each of these, it queries the insurance vector database to retrieve detailed policy texts, riders, and exclusions (up to 12 chunks per policy), and concatenates them into a rich context block. The node then builds an elaborate prompt that includes the full user profile, user preferences with importance ratings (extracted from the lifestyle string), the shortlisted plans, the retrieved policy documents, and the scorecard data (rubrics and weights). The LLM is instructed to re‑validate eligibility, compute final weighted scores, use the importance ratings as qualitative tie‑breakers, and perform a comparative analysis of the three plans. It must then select the best plan, justify with specific evidence from the policy texts, highlight trade‑offs honestly, and suggest an alternative. The output follows a strict format (BEST_PLAN, WHY THIS PLAN, TRADE-OFFS, ALTERNATIVE) with no extra text, ensuring a clear, actionable, and evidence‑based recommendation for term life insurance.",
                "lineHeight": 14,
                "fontSize": 11,
                "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
              },
              "lineHeight": 14,
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
            },
            "lineHeight": 14,
            "fontSize": 11,
            "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
          },
          "lineHeight": 14,
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
        },
        "lineHeight": 14,
        "fontSize": 11,
        "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "node_id": "node-term-insurance-recommendation-b0ba433c",
        "name": "Term Insurance Recommendation",
        "description": "Retrieves full policy texts for the top 3 shortlisted plans and builds a detailed term insurance recommendation prompt.\n\nThis node prepares a comprehensive prompt for an LLM to produce the single best term life insurance recommendation from a shortlist. It first parses the shortlisted policies (from the previous LLM output) to extract the names of the top three plans. For each of these, it queries the insurance vector database to retrieve detailed policy texts, riders, and exclusions (up to 12 chunks per policy), and concatenates them into a rich context block. The node then builds an elaborate prompt that includes the full user profile, user preferences with importance ratings (extracted from the lifestyle string), the shortlisted plans, the retrieved policy documents, and the scorecard data (rubrics and weights). The LLM is instructed to re‑validate eligibility, compute final weighted scores, use the importance ratings as qualitative tie‑breakers, and perform a comparative analysis of the three plans. It must then select the best plan, justify with specific evidence from the policy texts, highlight trade‑offs honestly, and suggest an alternative. The output follows a strict format (BEST_PLAN, WHY THIS PLAN, TRADE-OFFS, ALTERNATIVE) with no extra text, ensuring a clear, actionable, and evidence‑based recommendation for term life insurance.",
        "category": "llm",
        "owner_id": "105973339426953711978",
        "visibility": "public",
        "organization_id": 1,
        "edge_node": false,
        "live_version": "v1",
        "created_at": "2026-06-24 15:59:37.742387"
      },
