    {
      "id": "4gne4uhpz",
      "node_id": "node-context-generator-(mistral)-9bc89c39",
      "version_tag": "v1",
      "title": "Text Generate (Mistral)",
      "description": {
        "text": {
          "text": {
            "text": "This node performs text generation using a preloaded Mistral language model, turning an input prompt into a coherent response with configurable decoding behavior. The model and tokenizer are already provided by the wrapper, so the node focuses on preparing inputs and executing generation.\n\nIt first ensures the model has a valid GenerationConfig, initializing one from the model configuration if needed. The input prompt is then tokenized with padding and truncation, and all tensors are moved to the correct device for efficient inference.\n\nThe node calls the model’s generate method with parameters such as max_new_tokens (controls output length), temperature and top_p (control randomness and diversity), and do_sample (switches between deterministic and sampling-based generation). After generation, the output tokens are decoded into readable text with special tokens removed.\n\nThe final result is a clean text string representing the model’s response, ready for use in chat, completion, or downstream processing tasks.",
            "lineHeight": 14,
            "fontSize": 11,
            "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
          },
          "lineHeight": 14,
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
        },
        "lineHeight": 14,
        "fontSize": 11,
        "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "node_id": "node-context-generator-(mistral)-9bc89c39",
        "name": "Text Generate (Mistral)",
        "description": "This node performs text generation using a preloaded Mistral language model, turning an input prompt into a coherent response with configurable decoding behavior. The model and tokenizer are already provided by the wrapper, so the node focuses on preparing inputs and executing generation.\n\nIt first ensures the model has a valid GenerationConfig, initializing one from the model configuration if needed. The input prompt is then tokenized with padding and truncation, and all tensors are moved to the correct device for efficient inference.\n\nThe node calls the model’s generate method with parameters such as max_new_tokens (controls output length), temperature and top_p (control randomness and diversity), and do_sample (switches between deterministic and sampling-based generation). After generation, the output tokens are decoded into readable text with special tokens removed.\n\nThe final result is a clean text string representing the model’s response, ready for use in chat, completion, or downstream processing tasks.",
