    {
      "id": "59ndkgp2m",
      "node_id": "node-text-generate-(gemma)-0d5bdde2",
      "version_tag": "v1",
      "title": "Text Generate (Gemma)",
      "description": {
        "text": {
          "text": "This node performs text-only chat generation using a Gemma-style language model with structured conversation formatting. It supports both standard responses and optional “thinking” mode for more reasoning-oriented outputs.\nThe node constructs a chat-style input using a system prompt and user prompt, then formats it with the processor’s apply_chat_template, which prepares the text in the model’s expected conversational format. An optional enable_thinking flag can be used to activate internal reasoning behaviors (if supported by the model).\nThe formatted input is tokenized and sent to the model for generation using configurable sampling parameters:\n\n\nmax_new_tokens → controls response length\n\n\ntemperature, top_p, top_k → control randomness and diversity\n\n\ndo_sample → enables probabilistic generation\n\n\nAfter generation, only the newly generated portion (excluding the prompt) is decoded. The processor then parses the raw output into a clean final response, handling any structured formatting specific to Gemma models.\nThe result is a well-structured assistant reply, suitable for chat, reasoning tasks, or general text generation workflows.",
          "lineHeight": 14,
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
        },
        "lineHeight": 14,
        "fontSize": 11,
        "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "node_id": "node-text-generate-(gemma)-0d5bdde2",
        "name": "Text Generate (Gemma)",
        "description": "This node performs text-only chat generation using a Gemma-style language model with structured conversation formatting. It supports both standard responses and optional “thinking” mode for more reasoning-oriented outputs.\nThe node constructs a chat-style input using a system prompt and user prompt, then formats it with the processor’s apply_chat_template, which prepares the text in the model’s expected conversational format. An optional enable_thinking flag can be used to activate internal reasoning behaviors (if supported by the model).\nThe formatted input is tokenized and sent to the model for generation using configurable sampling parameters:\n\n\nmax_new_tokens → controls response length\n\n\ntemperature, top_p, top_k → control randomness and diversity\n\n\ndo_sample → enables probabilistic generation\n\n\nAfter generation, only the newly generated portion (excluding the prompt) is decoded. The processor then parses the raw output into a clean final response, handling any structured formatting specific to Gemma models.\nThe result is a well-structured assistant reply, suitable for chat, reasoning tasks, or general text generation workflows.",
