    {
      "id": "40fec293-72dc-4214-88f0-3d2934621230",
      "name": "term_insurance_scorecard",
      "resourceType": "variable",
      "description": "",
      "components": {
        "f86821d4": {
          "type": "string",
          "value": "# TERM INSURANCE SCORECARD – v1.0  ## RUBRICS (0–10 per criterion)  ### 1. Claim Settlement Ratio (CSR by count) Direct map from market_stats.csr_by_count_pct:   ≥99.5%   → 10   99-99.5% → 9   98-99%   → 8   97-98%   → 7   95-97%   → 6   92-95%   → 5   90-92%   → 4   <90%     → 2  ### 2. Premium Competitiveness Benchmark = annual premium for 30-year-old male non-smoker, ₹1 Cr sum assured, 30-year regular pay. Median of all policies in the table = ₹9,600 (2024 IRDAI reference). Score mapping:   ≤75% of median  → 10   ≤85% of median  → 8   ≤100% of median → 6   ≤115% of median → 4   >115% of median → 2  ### 3. Max Sum Assured (crore)   ≥50      → 10   25-50    → 9   10-25    → 8   5-10     → 6   2-5      → 4   <2       → 2 Bonus: +1 if HNI cover (≥10 Cr) offered without medical (if noted in notes)  ### 4. Entry / Maturity Age Range entry_score (max entry age):   ≥70 → 5, 60-69 → 4, 55-59 → 3, 50-54 → 2, <50 → 1 maturity_score (max maturity age):   ≥99 → 5, 85-98 → 4, 75-84 → 3, 65-74 → 2, <65 → 1 total = entry + maturity, capped at 10.  ### 5. Riders & Optional Benefits Each Y adds:   critical_illness_rider → 3   accidental_death_rider → 2   waiver_of_premium      → 2   permanent_disability   → 2   terminal_illness_inbuilt → 1   step_up_option         → 1   premium_break          → 1 Cap at 10.  ### 6. Premium Payment Flexibility Each Y adds:   regular_pay   → 2   limited_pay   → 2 (any limited pay option)   single_pay    → 1   return_of_premium → 2   premium_break → 1   modal_flex    → 1 (assume Y for all) Cap at 10.  ### 7. Insurer Solvency & Trust solvency_score (solvency_ratio):   ≥2.50 → 4, 2.00-2.50 → 3, 1.80-2.00 → 2, 1.50-1.80 → 1, <1.50 → 0 longevity_score (years_in_india):   ≥20 → 3, 10-20 → 2, 5-10 → 1, <5 → 0 amount_csr_score (csr_by_amount_pct):   ≥95% → 3, 90-95% → 2, 85-90% → 1, <85% → 0 total = solvency + longevity + amount_csr, capped at 10.  ## WEIGHTS (sum to 100)  Criterion                | Base | YoungSingle | FamilyBreadwinner | HNI | PreRetirement | Smoker -------------------------|------|-------------|-------------------|-----|---------------|-------- claim_settlement         | 30   | 25          | 35                | 25  | 35            | 35 premium_competitive      | 20   | 30          | 20                | 5   | 15            | 25 max_sum_assured          | 10   | 10          | 15                | 30  | 5             | 5 age_range                | 5    | 0           | 5                 | 5   | 20            | 5 riders                   | 15   | 10          | 15                | 15  | 10            | 15 premium_flexibility      | 10   | 15          | 5                 | 10  | 10            | 5 solvency_trust           | 10   | 10          | 5                 | 10  | 5             | 10  ## PROFILE SELECTION LOGIC (choose first match) if tobacco_user == true → use \"Smoker\" else if desired_sum_assured_crore >= 10 or annual_income_lakhs == \">50\" → use \"HNI\" else if age >= 45 and planning_retirement == true → use \"PreRetirement\" else if marital_status == \"married\" and dependents_count ≥ 1 → use \"FamilyBreadwinner\" else if age <= 30 and dependents_count == 0 → use \"YoungSingle\" else → use \"Base\"  ## HARD FILTERS (drop policy if any fails) - If desired_sum_assured_crore > max_sum_assured_crore → drop - If user.age > max_entry_age → drop - If user.age + desired_policy_term_years > max_maturity_age → drop - If tobacco_user == true and policy has no smoker discount/loading (assume allowed, but smoker profile uses different weight) - If want_rop == true and return_of_premium != \"Y\" → drop - If want_critical_illness == true and critical_illness_rider != \"Y\" → drop  ## POLICY ATTRIBUTES TABLE (simplified – key columns only) Columns: insurer | product | max_entry_age | max_maturity_age | max_sum_assured_crore | benchmark_premium_30m_ns_1cr_30y | critical_illness_rider | accidental_death_rider | waiver_of_premium | permanent_disability_rider | terminal_illness_inbuilt | step_up_option | premium_break | regular_pay | limited_pay | single_pay | return_of_premium  HDFC Life | Click 2 Protect Super | 84 | 85 | 200 | 9800 | N | N | N | N | Y | Y | N | Y | Y | Y | N HDFC Life | Click 2 Protect Life | 65 | 75 | 100 | 7900 | Y | N | N | N | Y | N | N | Y | Y | Y | N HDFC Life | Click 2 Protect Supreme | 65 | 85 | 100 | 9500 | Y | Y | Y | Y | Y | N | N | Y | Y | Y | N HDFC Life | Click 2 Protect Supreme Plus | 65 | 85 | 100 | 10500 | Y | Y | Y | Y | Y | N | N | Y | Y | Y | Y ICICI Prudential | iProtect Smart | 65 | 99 | 100 | 9500 | Y | Y | N | Y | Y | N | N | Y | Y | Y | N ICICI Prudential | iProtect Smart Plus | 65 | 85 | 100 | 9700 | N | Y | N | N | Y | Y | Y | Y | Y | Y | N ICICI Prudential | iProtect Smart Return of Premium | 65 | 75 | 50 | 18000 | N | N | N | N | Y | N | N | Y | Y | Y | Y Max Life | Smart Secure Plus | 65 | 85 | 100 | 9200 | Y | Y | Y | N | Y | Y | N | Y | Y | Y | Y Max Life | Smart Total Elite Protection | 65 | 99 | 200 | 11500 | Y | Y | N | N | Y | Y | N | Y | Y | Y | N Max Life | Smart Term Plan Plus | 65 | 85 | 100 | 9000 | Y | Y | Y | N | Y | Y | N | Y | Y | Y | Y Tata AIA | Sampoorna Raksha Supreme | 65 | 100 | 100 | 9800 | Y | Y | Y | Y | Y | N | N | Y | Y | Y | N Bajaj Allianz Life | Smart Protect Goal | 65 | 85 | 100 | 9600 | Y | Y | Y | Y | Y | N | N | Y | Y | Y | Y Aditya Birla Sun Life | DigiShield Plan | 65 | 99 | 100 | 9500 | Y | Y | Y | Y | Y | N | N | Y | Y | Y | Y Kotak Life | e-Term Plan | 65 | 85 | 100 | 9400 | Y | Y | Y | Y | Y | Y | N | Y | Y | Y | N PNB MetLife | Mera Term Plan Plus | 65 | 85 | 100 | 9700 | Y | Y | N | Y | Y | N | N | Y | Y | Y | Y LIC | New Tech-Term | 65 | 80 | 5 | 11500 | N | N | N | N | Y | N | N | Y | Y | Y | N LIC | Yuva Term | 45 | 75 | 5 | 8500 | N | N | N | N | Y | N | N | Y | Y | Y | N SBI Life | eShield Next | 65 | 80 | 100 | 9400 | Y | Y | N | N | Y | Y | N | Y | Y | Y | N  (Note: “regular_pay”, “limited_pay”, “single_pay”, “return_of_premium” are Y/N based on policy_attributes.)  ## MARKET STATS TABLE Columns: insurer | csr_by_count_pct | csr_by_amount_pct | solvency_ratio | years_in_india  HDFC Life | 99.5 | 98.65 | 1.87 | 25 ICICI Prudential | 99.17 | 97.45 | 2.04 | 25 Max Life | 99.65 | 98.74 | 1.92 | 25 LIC | 98.62 | 98.21 | 1.98 | 69 Tata AIA | 99.13 | 98.53 | 1.93 | 24 Bajaj Allianz Life | 99.04 | 97.10 | 4.49 | 24 Aditya Birla Sun Life | 98.10 | 96.50 | 1.86 | 24 Kotak Life | 98.82 | 97.42 | 2.69 | 24 PNB MetLife | 97.55 | 96.20 | 1.93 | 24 SBI Life | 98.39 | 97.12 | 2.21 | 24 Canara HSBC Life | 98.95 | 97.65 | 3.49 | 17 HSBC Life | 97.50 | 96.10 | 1.95 | 17 Bandhan Life | 99.66 | 97.95 | 1.85 | 17  ## FINAL SCORES quality = Σ(weight x criterion_score) / 10   (0-100) value   = quality / (annual_premium_in_thousands)   (use benchmark_premium if user premium not known)  ## NOTES - Always apply hard filters before scoring. - For missing attributes (e.g., rider not listed) assume N. - Premium competitiveness uses the benchmark premium column – do not invent. - Output only top 5 policies with their quality scores.",
